    <briefdescription>
<para>Implements conversion of HPCToolkit XML tree representation to the <ref refid="namespaceRoseHPCT" kindref="compound">RoseHPCT</ref> IR representation. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This class uses a pre-order traversal, maintaining the following invariants during the traversal:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>saved_parents_ is the list of nodes whose children are still being processed.</para></listitem><listitem><para>At each call to &apos;visit ()&apos;, saved_parents_.top () is the current node&apos;s parent.</para></listitem><listitem><para>The first node pushed onto saved_parents_ is the root program node of the XML tree.</para></listitem><listitem><para>When a &apos;metric&apos; node is encountered, &apos;visit ()&apos; pushes a dummy node (NULL) onto the list of parents, since metrics are not explicitly represented by IR nodes but rather attached to IR nodes.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para><simplesect kind="note"><para>After each traversal, the user is responsible for deleting the new IR tree. </para></simplesect>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
